ue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.363986,39.4100985]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[4009.6,5476.8],"name":"3rd Street North / East Beach Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3628981,39.4102062]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[5021.5,5549.1],"name":"4th Street North / East Beach Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3621357,39.4105785]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[6687.2,2967.1],"name":"6th Street North / Quay Boulevard"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3622811,39.4127172]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[7837.3,3892.9],"name":"7th Street North / Quay Boulevard"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3609751,39.4126366]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[3839.3,622.9],"name":"Quay Boulevard / Sheridan Place"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3655726,39.412879]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[7009.5,5254.0],"name":"6th Street North / East Beach Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3608633,39.4115399]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[8002.4,5113.6],"name":"7th Street North / East Beach Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3602224,39.4120162]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[7935.9,2631.4],"name":"East Evans Boulevard / Heald Road"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3615721,39.4133608]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[3455.4,4310.1],"name":"East Evans Boulevard / Lafayette Place"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3639204,39.4106493]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[415.3,1597.2],"name":"Girard Place / Lafayette Place"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3675602,39.4109542]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[6010.2,5393.4],"name":"5th Street North / East Beach Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3615041,39.4110627]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[496.4,4536.9],"name":"2nd Street South / Sheridan Place / West Evans Boulevard"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3659744,39.4093555]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[5314.7,7667.8],"name":"4th Street North / East Brigantine Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3608317,39.4095156]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[4330.3,7799.4],"name":"3rd Street North / East Brigantine Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3614758,39.4090415]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1874.0,2982.8],"name":"Lafayette Place / South Roosevelt Boulevard"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3657733,39.4107712]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[382.1,8626.4],"name":"2nd Street South / West Brigantine Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.3639301,39.4069927]}}]}}},"metadata":{"sheet-2":{"description":"The southwestern end of the built-up grid of Brigantine City, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, from 33rd Street South west to 40th Street South and from Bay Shore Avenue across Brigantine Avenue to Ocean Avenue and the bulkhead on the Atlantic Ocean. North of Bay Shore Avenue the sheet shows the bay-side tracts along Absecon Inlet and Bonita Tideway: Adams, Amherst, Erie and Jackson Avenues (Amherst, Erie and part of Jackson marked not opened), the large unbuilt blocks 255, 256 and 257 with a sewage disposal plant, and the diagonal Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard running to a traffic circle at Bay Shore Avenue, where an observation tower stands, with a fire alarm box, a gasoline station, a steel water tower on a 100 ft tower (15,000 gallons) and a garage for twenty cars with a concrete floor. The residential blocks 99 to 106 and 124 to 131 are platted in narrow lots with only a scattering of frame dwellings, and the beach blocks 220 to 227 south of Ocean Avenue are empty except for a bath house in block 221. Water pipes run along Bay Shore, Brigantine and Ocean Avenues and down several cross streets, with hydrants marked. The cross streets above and below Brigantine Avenue do not line up exactly at 39th and 40th Streets. A scale bar is drawn in Ocean Avenue at 40th Street.","notes":["The 1927 traffic circle where Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard meets Bay Shore Avenue is today's Brigantine Circle; the boulevard west of it is now Brigantine Boulevard.","Jackson Avenue and Adams Avenue are not in the OpenStreetMap extract; Erie and part of Amherst Avenue are marked not opened.","Bay Shore Avenue is drawn 50 to 60 ft wide; the modern parcels give about 97 ft, and its junctions carry 3 to 7 m residuals.","West of 36th Street South the cross streets are drawn about 33 ft wide south of Brigantine Avenue and 50 ft north of it, and do not line up across Brigantine Avenue; blocks south of Brigantine Avenue have a 20 ft alley.","100 ft. 33rd to 40th Street South, Bay Shore Av to Ocean Av; bay-side tracts (Adams, Amherst, Erie, Jackson Avs) and Atlantic-Brigantine Blvd with traffic circle (now Brigantine Circle). One part. West of 36th the cross streets are drawn about 33 ft wide below Brigantine Av (50 ft above) and jog at Brigantine Av; with a 20 ft alley in each block they mislead the detector. Second-order fit, 2.8 m RMSE / 4.0 m LOO; 38th to 40th / Ocean excluded (misdetected or on the scale bar). Medium-low confidence."],"streetnames":["Bay Shore Avenue","Brigantine Avenue","Ocean Avenue","Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard","Adams Avenue","Amherst Avenue","Erie Avenue","Jackson Avenue","33rd Street South","34th Street South","35th Street South","36th Street South","37th Street South","38th Street South","39th Street South","40th Street South"],"placenames":["Absecon Inlet","Bonita Tideway","Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-3":{"description":"Residential blocks of Brigantine City between 33rd and 26th Streets South, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, from Bay Shore Avenue across Revere Boulevard and Brigantine Avenue to Ocean Avenue and the bulkhead on the Atlantic Ocean. Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard enters at the upper left and runs diagonally to Brigantine Avenue near 30th Street, cutting the blocks between 33rd and 31st Streets into irregular shapes; Revere Boulevard begins east of it. Blocks 107 to 114, 132 to 136 and 228 to 235 are laid out in narrow numbered lots with a few scattered frame dwellings and garages, and the beach blocks 212 to 219 south of Ocean Avenue are mostly empty. At the upper left, block 233 holds the yard of John Murtland Inc., builders' supplies, with a storage shed and office; a gasoline station stands at the boulevard near 33rd Street. Water pipes of 4 to 8 inches run along the avenues and cross streets, with hydrants marked. The bulkhead along the ocean front steps out east of 29th Street, and a board walk is noted at 29th Street.","notes":["Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard has been realigned: its modern line runs east-west near the old 33rd to 29th Street blocks instead of diagonally to Brigantine Avenue; it was left out of the control.","Brigantine Avenue here is West Brigantine Avenue today.","John Murtland Inc., builders' supplies, block 233.","100 ft. 26th to 33rd Street South, Bay Shore Av to Ocean Av; Atlantic-Brigantine Blvd diagonal (realigned since, left out). One part."],"streetnames":["Bay Shore Avenue","Revere Boulevard","Brigantine Avenue","Ocean Avenue","Atlantic-Brigantine Boulevard","26th Street South","27th Street South","28th Street South","29th Street South","30th Street South","31st Street South","32nd Street South","33rd Street South"],"placenames":["Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-4":{"description":"Residential blocks of Brigantine City from 26th Street South east to 18th Street South, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, from Bay Shore Avenue, which angles across the upper right corner, across Revere Boulevard and Brigantine Avenue to Ocean Avenue and the bulkhead on the Atlantic Ocean. Blocks 114 to 121 and 136 to 143 are divided into narrow lots, with frame dwellings and garages scattered through them, a few more densely between 25th and 23rd Streets; blocks 239 to 241 lie north of Bay Shore Avenue. South of Ocean Avenue, blocks 205 to 212 run to the bulkhead; between 19th and 18th Streets the beach blocks 205 and 206 are drawn without cross streets. Water pipes of 4 to 8 inches run along the avenues and cross streets, with hydrants marked. The sheet carries a north arrow and a scale bar in the lower right.","notes":["Brigantine Avenue here is West Brigantine Avenue today.","100 ft. 18th to 25th Street South (26th at left edge), Bay Shore Av to Ocean Av. One part."],"streetnames":["Bay Shore Avenue","Revere Boulevard","Brigantine Avenue","Ocean Avenue","18th Street South","19th Street South","20th Street South","21st Street South","22nd Street South","23rd Street South","24th Street South","25th Street South"],"placenames":["Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-5":{"description":"The centre of Brigantine City in 1927, from 18th Street South east to 10th Street South, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, from Bonita Cove and Bay Shore Avenue across Revere Boulevard and Brigantine Avenue to Ocean Avenue and the Atlantic Ocean beach. Bay Shore Avenue curves along the cove shore at the top and becomes Beach Avenue east of about 14th Street; Revere Boulevard runs from the left edge to 15th Street. Block 31, between 15th and 14th Streets, holds the public school (heated by steam, electric lights) and City Hall; across Brigantine Avenue a private garage stands on 15th Street. On the beach front between 15th and 14th Streets is the Hotel Brigantine, a fireproof steel-frame building with reinforced concrete floors, built 1926 and closed in winter with a caretaker living in the building, with a bath house beside it and a drive running south toward the Brigantine Pier, noted as 450 ft away and shown on sheet 6. The other blocks (11 to 16, 27 to 32, 122 to 123, 144 to 145, 242 to 246) are platted in narrow lots with few buildings, and the beach blocks 197 to 204 are empty. Water pipes and hydrants are marked along the streets, with a fire alarm box at 15th Street.","notes":["Hotel Brigantine, built 1926, closed in winter.","Public School and City Hall in block 31.","Beach Avenue here is West Beach Avenue today; Brigantine Avenue is West Brigantine Avenue.","100 ft. 10th to 18th Street South, Bonita Cove and Bay Shore / Beach Av to Ocean Av; Public School, City Hall, Hotel Brigantine. One part."],"streetnames":["Bay Shore Avenue","Beach Avenue","Revere Boulevard","Brigantine Avenue","Ocean Avenue","10th Street South","11th Street South","12th Street South","13th Street South","14th Street South","15th Street South","16th Street South","17th Street South","18th Street South"],"placenames":["Bonita Cove","Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-6-1":{"description":"Blocks of Brigantine City from 10th Street South east to 2nd Street South, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, from Evans Boulevard at the top across Beach Avenue and Brigantine Avenue to the ocean front. North of Beach Avenue, Sheridan Square and Georgia Place meet at a small circle between 8th and 7th Streets in a group of four large blocks numbered 500; Evans Boulevard turns diagonally across the upper right corner. Between 10th and 8th Streets the grid continues to Ocean Avenue and the beach blocks 195 and 196, while east of 8th Street the ocean has cut into the shore and the beach blocks 300 to 305 run straight from Brigantine Avenue to the water. In block 300 stands St. Thomas Catholic Chapel (drawn from plans), and near 7th Street a U.S. Coast Guard boat house. Most blocks are platted in narrow lots with a scattering of frame dwellings; block 404, between 4th and 3rd Streets, has a row of small buildings coloured as stone or concrete and a private garage. Water pipes of 4 to 10 inches run along the avenues. The lower part of the sheet is taken up by three insets framed by heavy lines, which are separate parts.","notes":["St. Thomas Catholic Chapel, block 300, drawn from plans.","U.S. Coast Guard boat house near 7th Street South.","Evans Boulevard here is West Evans Boulevard today; Beach and Brigantine Avenues are West Beach and West Brigantine Avenues.","100 ft. Part 1 (main): 2nd to 10th Street South, Evans Blvd to the ocean; St. Thomas Catholic Chapel, Coast Guard boat house. Part 2 (inset, lower left): blocks 422, 701, 702 at 14th and 15th Streets North on Brigantine Av. Part 3 (inset, lower centre): blocks 19 to 22 at 19th to 21st Streets North, Beach Av to Brigantine Av. Part 4 (inset, lower right): Brigantine Pier with auditorium.","Not georeferenced on this sheet: inset: blocks 19 to 22, 19th to 21st Streets North between Beach and Brigantine Avenues (no street junction: 19th to 21st Streets North no longer exist (north end of the island)).","Not georeferenced on this sheet: inset: Brigantine Pier with auditorium (no street junction; pier gone; needs step 6b: pier is 450 ft from the Hotel Brigantine (sheet-5); only the board walk line and that distance tie it to land)."],"streetnames":["Evans Boulevard","Georgia Place","Sheridan Square","Beach Avenue","Brigantine Avenue","Ocean Avenue","2nd Street South","3rd Street South","4th Street South","5th Street South","6th Street South","7th Street South","8th Street South","9th Street South","10th Street South"],"placenames":["Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-6-2":{"description":"A small inset at the lower left of sheet 6, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, showing three blocks on the ocean side of Brigantine Avenue at the north end of the island: block 422 (key 3A) west of 14th Street North, block 701 (key 4A) between 14th and 15th Streets North, and the edge of block 702 east of 15th Street North. Brigantine Avenue, 100 feet wide with a 10 inch water pipe, runs along the bottom edge and only its near side is drawn. Block 422 has a frame dwelling and outbuildings near Brigantine Avenue; block 701 has a store, two dwellings and a storage shed along Brigantine Avenue, with lots numbered 1001 to 1006. The rest of the blocks is empty. The inset has its own north arrow, at about the same angle as the main map.","notes":["Placed on one junction (14th Street North / East Brigantine Avenue) with the atlas scale and the rotation of its drawn lines: low confidence.","15th Street North no longer meets Brigantine Avenue at its 1927 position.","100 ft. Part 1 (main): 2nd to 10th Street South, Evans Blvd to the ocean; St. Thomas Catholic Chapel, Coast Guard boat house. Part 2 (inset, lower left): blocks 422, 701, 702 at 14th and 15th Streets North on Brigantine Av. Part 3 (inset, lower centre): blocks 19 to 22 at 19th to 21st Streets North, Beach Av to Brigantine Av. Part 4 (inset, lower right): Brigantine Pier with auditorium.","Not georeferenced on this sheet: inset: blocks 19 to 22, 19th to 21st Streets North between Beach and Brigantine Avenues (no street junction: 19th to 21st Streets North no longer exist (north end of the island)).","Not georeferenced on this sheet: inset: Brigantine Pier with auditorium (no street junction; pier gone; needs step 6b: pier is 450 ft from the Hotel Brigantine (sheet-5); only the board walk line and that distance tie it to land)."],"streetnames":["Brigantine Avenue","14th Street North","15th Street North"]},"sheet-7-1":{"description":"The northeastern part of Brigantine City in 1927, drawn at 100 feet to an inch, around Penn Circle, where Roosevelt Boulevard, Evans Boulevard and Beach Avenue meet. North and west of the circle a radiating plan of named places fills the sheet: Girard, Franklin, Sheridan, Lafayette, Putnam and Hamilton Places, Quay Boulevard and Heald Road, with blocks 603 to 613 and the triangular plots B and C, almost entirely unbuilt. South of the circle, Roosevelt Boulevard (100 feet wide) and Vernon Place run down to Brigantine Avenue, and east of it the numbered streets 2nd to 7th Street North cross Beach Avenue and Brigantine Avenue in blocks 406 to 414 and 505 to 512, with curving blocks 506 to 509 between Evans Boulevard and Beach Avenue. Buildings are few: the fire department in block 411 on 4th Street North, a pump house in block 407, a fire alarm box and a row of small two-storey offices at Roosevelt Boulevard and Brigantine Avenue, and scattered dwellings. Beach blocks 306 to 313 run from Brigantine Avenue to the Atlantic Ocean. The lower right corner is an inset (a separate part) showing blocks at 39th to 41st Streets North.","notes":["Penn Circle no longer exists as drawn; the modern Evans Boulevard, Beach Avenue and Roosevelt Boulevard junctions around it did not detect.","Several modern streets carry two nodes at one junction (Sheridan Place / South Roosevelt Boulevard); one was excluded.","Fire department in block 411 on 4th Street North.","100 ft. Part 1 (main): Penn Circle area, Girard to Heald Rd, 2nd Street South to 7th Street North, Bay Shore to the ocean. Part 2 (inset, lower right): blocks 703 to 705 at 39th to 41st Streets North with the U.S. Coast Guard Station, Brigantine Av not opened.","Not georeferenced on this sheet: inset: blocks 703 to 705, 39th to 41st Streets North, U.S. Coast Guard Station (no street junction: 39th to 41st Streets North and this part of Brigantine Avenue no longer exist)."],"streetnames":["Bay Shore Avenue","Girard Place","Franklin Place","Roosevelt Boulevard","Sheridan Place","Lafayette Place","Putnam Place","Hamilton Place","Quay Boulevard","Heald Road","Evans Boulevard","Penn Circle","Beach Avenue","Vernon Place","Brigantine Avenue","2nd Street South","2nd Street North","3rd Street North","4th Street North","5th Street North","6th Street North","7th Street North"],"placenames":["Atlantic Ocean"]}}}